---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import balrogImage from '../assets/images/style/gothmog.jpg';

const pageTitle = "Style - Thamara Kandabada";
const slashpageImage = "/featured-images/style.png";
---
<PageLayout title={pageTitle} image={slashpageImage}>
  <h1>Style</h1>
    <p>On this page you can see how different elements are styled on this website. I have not used any pre-packaged themes; all CSS was handwritten from the ground up.</p>
    <p>While this website is designed to be fully responsive using media queries, it is best viewed on desktop.</p>
    <h2 id="colour-palette">Colour palette</h2>
      <p>I have opted for a simple colour palette that skews dark, without giving the site a stark contrast. There is currently no light mode.</p>
        <div class="colour-palette-box">
          <div class="primary-bg">
            <p>Primary background <Code code={`#16213E`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="secondary-bg">
            <p>Secondary background <Code code={`#161B22`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="tertiary-bg">
            <p>Tertiary background <Code code={`#21262D`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="primary-text">
            <p>Primary text <Code code={`#CBD5E1`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="secondary-text">
            <p>Secondary text <Code code={`#94A3B8`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="border">
            <p>Border colour <Code code={`#E94560`} inline /></p>
          </div>
          <div class="accent">
            <p>Accent colour <Code code={`#4DA8DA`} inline /></p>
          </div>
        </div>
    <h2 id="typography">Typography</h2>
      <p>This site uses three typefaces from <a href="https://www.indiantypefoundry.com/" target="_blank">Indian Type Foundry</a>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://www.fontshare.com/fonts/erode" target="_blank">Erode</a> is used for headings.</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.fontshare.com/fonts/plein" target="_blank">Plein</a> is used for body text.</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.fontshare.com/fonts/jet-brains-mono" target="_blank">JetBrains Mono</a> is used for code blocks and inline code.</li>
        </ul>
      <p>I am self-hosting these fonts. The variable font weights are used to create variations in text appearance as necessary.</p>
        <div class="grid-box">
          <h1>Heading 1</h1>
            <p>Level 1 headings are set in Erode and the primary text colour, and have the following properties:</p>
            <p>Font size: <Code code={`2.8rem`} inline />, Font weight: <Code code={`500`} inline /></p>
          <h2>Heading 2</h2>
            <p>Level 2 headings are set in Erode and the secondary text colour, and have the following properties:</p>
            <p>Font size: <Code code={`1.8rem`} inline />, Font weight: <Code code={`700`} inline /></p>
            <p>They are also styled with a trailing line that extends the full remaining width of the container and is set in the border colour.</p>
          <h3>Heading 3</h3>
            <p>Level 3 headings are set in Erode and the primary text colour, and have the following properties:</p>
            <p>Font size: <Code code={`1.65rem`} inline />, Font weight: <Code code={`500`} inline /></p>
          <h4>Heading 4</h4>
            <p>Level 4 headings are set in Erode and the secondary text colour, and have the following properties:</p>
            <p>Font size: <Code code={`1.4rem`} inline />, Font weight: <Code code={`400`} inline /></p>
        </div>
      <p><Code code={`h5`} inline /> and <Code code={`h6`} inline /> titles are not used on this website.</p>
      <p>Paragraph text is set in Plein at <Code code={`1.1rem`} inline />. List elements share the font size. </p>
      <p>Inline <Code code={`a`} inline /> elements in the body are set in the secondary text colour. They are decorated with a <Code code={`1px`} inline /> thick underline set in the border colour. On hover, the font weight changes to <Code code={`700`} inline />, while the font colour and the underline colour changes to the accent colour.</p>
      <p>Navigation links in the header and footer simply transition from the primary text colour to the accent colour on hover and do no have a background.</p>
      <p>Some linked elements resize using the <Code code={`transform: scale()`} inline /> function on hover. The posts list in the <a href="/notebook">Notebook</a> is an example of this.</p>
      <p>The monospace font JetBrains Mono is used for all code. It is set at <Code code={`0.9rem`} inline />.</p>
      <p>Code blocks are also enclosed in a background block with a border radius of <Code code={`4px`} inline /> and <Code code={`1rem`} inline /> padding. Overflow on the x-axis triggers a scrollbar. Syntax highlighting is handled by the built-in <a href="https://shiki.style/" target="_blank">Shiki</a> integration. I'm using the default <em>GitHub Dark</em> theme from Shiki, and this does not currently switch to a light theme when the website theme is toggled.</p>
      <p>See an example below:</p>
        <Code lang="css" code={
          `/*Overriding the width and height specification required by Astro's <Picture /> tag and adding a border radius*/
            img {
              max-width: 100%;
              height: auto;
              display: block;
              border-radius: 4px;
            }`
          }
        />
      <p>Inline code snippets are enclosed in a background block with a border radius of <Code code={`4px`} inline /> and <Code code={`0.15rem 0.25rem`} inline /> padding. They also have a <Code code={`1px`} inline /> dotted border set in the accent colour. Within markdown files, this background block is set in the tertiary background colour, however, within all other pages of the website, the Shiki colour theme takes over.</p>
      <p>Blockquotes are set in Erode and are italicised. They are <Code code={`1.5rem`} inline /> in font size and styled in the secondary text colour, with a <Code code={`1px`} inline /> left border styled in the accent colour. Blockquotes are only used for quotations rather than as a decorative element. See example below. </p>
        <blockquote>
          Arise, arise, Riders of Théoden!<br>Fell deeds awake: fire and slaughter!<br>Spear shall be shaken, shield be splintered,<br>a sword-day, a red day, ere the sun rises!<br>Ride now, ride now! Ride to Gondor!
        </blockquote>
      <p>Unordered lists use the default <Code code={`disc`} inline /> style and ordered lists use the default <Code code={`decimal`} inline /> style. Font colours are inherited from the parent. This is illustrated below.</p>
        <div class="grid-box grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Meals of the day</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Breakfast</li>
                <li>Second breakfast</li>
                <li>Elevenses</li>
                <li>Luncheon</li>
                <li>Afternoon Tea</li>
                <li>Dinner</li>
                <li>Supper</li>
              </ol>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Ways to prepare taters</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Boil 'em</li>
                <li>Mash 'em</li>
                <li>Stick 'em in a stew</li>
              </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      <p>All text, except blog post titles, is left-aligned. Blog post titles are centre-aligned with a background set in the secondary background colour, on which the hero image (if available) overlaps with a <Code code={`-120px`} inline /> vertical spacing. See an example <a href="/notebook/2026/08/life-in-objects">here</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="images">Images</h2>
      <p>All images are served in AVIF with fallback to WebP, feature a <Code code={`4px`} inline /> border radius, and include alt text. Captions, when used, are right-aligned and italicised. They are set in a font size of <Code code={`1rem`} inline /> and in the secondary text colour.</p>
      <p>All images have a subtle shadow, set to the values <Code code={`rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35) 0px 5px 15px`} inline />.</p>
      <p>See example below.</p>
        <figure>
          <Picture
            src={balrogImage}
            alt="A colourful and stylised drawing of a Balrog, engulfed in flames and wielding a large axe, riding a dragon"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          />
          <figcaption>
            Gothmog, Lord of the Balrogs, riding a dragon. <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GOTHMOG-1_(detail).jpg" target="_blank">Tttom</a>, <a href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      <p>Linked images, like the 88x31 buttons in the footer, move up by <Code code={`4px`} inline /> on hover using the <Code code={`translateY()`} inline /> function.</p>
    <h2 id="tables">Tables</h2>
      <p>Tables have a <Code code={`1px`} inline /> thick solid border set in the border colour with no border radius. The background of the header row is styled in the secondary background colour, while other rows have a transparent background. All text is left-aligned and vertically aligned to the top.</p>
      <p>See an example below:</p>
        <h3>Kings of Gondor</h3>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                <th scope="col">Reign</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Elendil</td>
                <td>Second Age 3320 – Second Age 3441</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Anárion</td>
                <td>Second Age 3320 – Second Age 3340</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Isildur</td>
                <td>Second Age 3320 – Third Age 2</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
    <h2 id="other-components">Other components</h2>
      <p>Grid elements have a <Code code={`1px`} inline /> thick solid border set in the border colour, with a <Code code={`4px`} inline /> border radius. The background is styled in the tertiary background colour. If the grid element is hyperlinked, the border transitions to the accent colour and the entire element moves up by <Code code={`4px`} inline /> on hover using the <Code code={`translateY()`} inline /> function.</p>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="grid-box">
            <p>This is an example of an unlinked grid element. See this in use on the <a href="/uses">Uses</a> page.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-box">

            <p>This is an example of a linked grid element. See this in use on the <a href="/projects/debas">Debas Archives</a> page.</p>

          </div>
        </div>
      <p><a href="https://indieweb.org/post_footer" target="_blank">Post footers</a> share the above styles (with the exception of the hover effect). On ordered lists inside post footers, numbers are styled in the accent colour. See example below.</p>
        <div class="post-footer">
          <p><strong>Further reading</strong> (courtesy of <a href="https://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/Reading_order" target="_blank">Tolkien Gateway</a>)</p>
            <ol id="post-footer-list">
              <li><span><em>The Silmarillion:</em> The Silmarillion describes the beginnings of Tolkien's world.</span></li>
              <li><span><em>The Hobbit:</em> Although directly unrelated to The Silmarillion, it is the next big story.</span></li>  
              <li><span><em>The Lord of the Rings:</em> The conclusion of the story of The Hobbit as well as things mentioned in The Silmarillion.</span></li>  
            </ol>
        </div>
    <h2 id="not-in-use">Currently not in use</h2>
      <p>I'm currently not using accordions and definition lists within this website.</p>
</PageLayout>